<title>DENMARK: POLL - 1998 EPS of top 20 Danish shares seen 8pct up.</title>
<headline>POLL - 1998 EPS of top 20 Danish shares seen 8pct up.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ten analysts polled by Reuters in a survey released on Tuesday forecast average rises of 6.1 percent in 1997 earnings per share (EPS), rising to 7.9 percent for 1998 for stocks on the Copenhagen Stock Exchange's KFX top-20 index.</p>
<p>In the last poll one month ago, the analyst panel forecast average EPS rises of 4.6 percent and 9.9 percent respectively for 1997 and 1998 EPS.</p>
<p>Topping the list with the highest expected EPS gains were energy and shipping group A.P. Moeller's D/S 1912 and D/S Svendborg which were forecast to register 1997 earnings per share 64 and 56 percent respectively up on the previous year.</p>
<p>Among the shares with the lowest expectations was Scandinavian Airlines (SAS), whose EPS the panel saw falling by almost half to 6.2 crowns in 1997 from 13.2 crowns in 1996, with leading banks Den Danske Bank, Unidanmark and BG Bank also seen as disappointing.</p>
